Source audit found two Phase 11 gaps. The Phase 9 matrix assigned Pull allocation/listener/registration/queues-in-balance APIs to this phase, but the Rust Pull facade had no assignment lifecycle. Also, Java `RebalanceImpl.rebalanceByTopic` checks a missing or empty local route before consumer membership; the Rust Push path queried membership first and treated an available empty route differently. Corrected the Push route order and added an empty-route regression test.

Implemented Pull rebalance config/API and runtime owner: Java-default average strategy and `enableRebalance`, queue-listener configuration/registration, namespaced topics/subscriptions, coalesced runtime rebalance trigger, client/broadcast assignment, safe offset removal/persist retry, live assignment query with Java namespace removal, and shutdown fencing. Added runtime tests for Pull broadcasting, clustering/membership unavailable retention, configuration and public lifecycle/query behavior. Focused consumer package test run passed before the additional clustering test; final full validation remains pending.

